# Backend build context — the image is built from `backend/` (backend/Dockerfile
# ends with `COPY . .`), so this list is the only gate that keeps development
# state out of a built image (PUB-07). The runtime inputs (app/, alembic/,
# alembic.ini, docker-entrypoint.sh, indramesh/, plugin_alembic/,
# plugin-requirements.txt, pyproject.toml, pytest.ini, requirements.txt,
# start.sh) are deliberately absent from it and must stay in the context.
#
# Matching note (moby/patternmatcher, verified): a pattern without `**` is
# anchored at the context root, so `__pycache__/` covers `backend/__pycache__`
# only. Every artifact below that also occurs further down the tree therefore
# carries a `**/` companion — without one, `app/__pycache__` or the first-run
# `app/_setup_user.pwd` would still be copied into the image.

# Test tree — never shipped, and the fixtures under tests/fixtures carry captured
# provider payloads with real identity data.
tests/

# Coverage artifacts from `coverage`/`pytest-cov`, plus the pytest cache.
.coverage
.coverage.*
**/.coverage
**/.coverage.*
.pytest_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/

# Bytecode caches.
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
**/*.pyc

# First-run password files and dotenv files — a built image must never bake in a
# credential.
*.pwd
**/*.pwd
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Static-analysis allowlist — an input for `vulture` runs, not for the service.
vulture_whitelist.py

# One-off probe and audit tooling (probe_jira_*.py, es-golden fixtures) — never
# executed in the image; backend/scripts is also excluded from the public mirror.
scripts/
